penguin-cpp (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Penguin cpp's own manual, in Spanish and English: F1, the Help menu
    and the dialogs' help buttons open it (it replaces Dev-C++'s, which
    spoke of Windows). It is also at
    https://juanfrang.github.io/Penguin-cpp/manual/
  * The Help menu says Penguin cpp, not Dev-C++.
  * macOS: one-line installer, astyle inside the app, Option-Space for
    code completion, and fixes in the lldb debugger.

 -- Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0500

penguin-cpp (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Penguin cpp also runs on macOS (Apple Silicon), from the same code.
  * The debug panel's end-of-program line no longer repeats the terminal's
    "press Enter to close this window".

 -- Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0500

penguin-cpp (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release of Penguin cpp, the Linux port of Dev-C++:
    - Editor with syntax colors, code completion, folding and class browser.
    - Single files and projects built with the system's gcc and make.
    - Programs run in a terminal window.
    - Debugger on top of gdb: breakpoints, watches, call stack, step by step.
    - Formatting with astyle and clang-format, printing and PDF export.

 -- Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0500
